    "extraction_status": "ready_for_resolution",
    "extraction_notes": "Single SoA table (ISA Section 1.3) printed over document pages 9-11 under a header (with the shaded Telephone Visit row and the Procedures band) reprinted on every page; p.8 carries the Section 1.3 heading and the intro text, captured as table-wide note g1. The table pages are glyph-spread (one token per glyph or glyph group): every activity label and Notes cell was rebuilt from the glyph stream and read again against the rendered page (§1c). Marks verified by pdftotext -bbox column binning (no disagreement with the visual read). Cell boundaries from raster rule lines (§1d). Notes column cells captured as annotations with synthesised markers n1-n18 (six cells split by the sentences that name visits); the printed footnotes a and b on the Telephone Visit mark are defined inside that row's Notes cell. Abbreviation list dropped. Redaction: the Telephone Visit Notes cell (end of footnotes a and b), one full row on p.11, and the Notes cell of 'Participant returns device'.",
    "model": "claude-opus-5-5"
  },
  "table_metadata": {
    "table_number": 1,
    "table_type": "main_soa",
    "table_title": "Schedule of Activities (SoA)",
    "table_purpose": "ISA BP03 (LY3556050, chronic low back pain) schedule: visits and procedures unique to the ISA, on top of the master CPMP and CLBP DSA CPMP(2) SoAs; V3-V7 and ED shared with the master, two telephone visits after V3 added, no follow-up visits",
    "page_start": 8,
    "page_end": 11,
    "notes": "One label column (L=1); data columns at positions 2-7 (V3 -> 2, V4 -> 3, V5 -> 4, V6 -> 5, V7 -> 6, ED -> 7); the right-hand Notes column is not a schedule column. The shaded 'Telephone Visit' row is printed with the header on every page and is recorded as header row 5 (see review item D1). The 'Procedures' band under it is reprinted on every page: a column-label band, not an activity (row position 6, left out). Typed main_soa: every participant randomised into this ISA passes through it in sequence. It is a delta schedule: the intro text says it shows only what is unique to the ISA, so the participant's full schedule is this table plus the master and DSA SoAs; recorded here and in g1. Section bands 'Laboratory Tests and Sample Collection' and 'Participant Device' group the rows below them. One fully redacted row (CCI) before the 'Participant Device' band; its row position (25) is unassigned."
  },
